# Test: show mtu answers one document every pipe renders
# Spec: spec-path-mtu-diagnostic -- user story 4, AC-19
# VALIDATES: the payload the RPC answers is one kebab-case document whose lists
#            are lists and whose identifiers carry no marker, which is what
#            `| json`, `| yaml` and `| table` each render (the three renderings
#            of the same document are pinned by
#            TestShowMTUEveryPipeRendersOnePayload in internal/component/mtu/cmd).
# PREVENTS: a payload pre-formatted as text, a snake_case key, or a verdict
#           glued to a name.
#
# The path is three network namespaces joined by veth pairs, built by the
# compiled fixture `plugin/clamped-path` (internal/test/fixture, netlink): the
# daemon runs in the sender namespace, the router forwards with its far link at
# 1400, and the far namespace answers. Building them needs CAP_NET_ADMIN and
# the raw ICMP socket needs CAP_NET_RAW, so the test runs in the QEMU guest as
# root (`./le qemu all-tests`) and skips in the unprivileged merge gate. The
# fixture removes the namespaces when the daemon exits, whatever its exit code.

option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw

tmpfs=mtu-json.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external show-mtu-test {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/show-mtu-json"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/clamped-path netns zemtujson$PORT run ze start mtu-json.conf:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show mtu answers one kebab-case document with its lists as lists
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
